/bg run now marks a job finished when its shell exits, even if something the job started in the background is still holding the output pipe. Build, clippy, fmt and the full cargo test all pass. It's committed as 318ea3e0 with "Fixes #1063", but not pushed yet; the push will close #1063.

Before and after: I wrote the test first and ran it on the old code. A job running sleep 8 & echo hi was still "running" after 4 seconds, and the test failed. That's because the old code read output until the pipe closed before it waited for the shell. It now waits for the shell first, then gives the output readers 2 seconds to drain, the same as /run and /watch.

One difference from `/run` and `/watch`, on purpose: in those two, the reader stops keeping output once the grace runs out. In /bg it keeps reading, because the output is read later. If a background process still holds the pipe, /bg output shows a one-line note and then anything that process writes afterwards, under the same 256KB cap. So I kept the grace at 2 seconds rather than making it longer: here it only controls how long the job shows as "running", not what gets captured. The background process is never killed.

Tests:
• New tests cover the held-open case and the output written after the note.
• Near-miss cases show no note:
  • echo hi; exit 3 gives exactly the same output and exit code as before.
  • A burst of output written just before exit is all kept.
  • A background process with its output redirected finishes quickly.
• I made the fix ineffective on purpose (grace raised to 600s, marked NEUTERED, restored in the same command). The two held-open tests failed by name, and all seven /bg tests passed again after restoring.

New bug, filed as #1077 and not fixed here: /bg kill reports the job as killed, but the shell keeps running. I checked this with a throwaway test: the process was still alive 500ms after kill() returned true. The cause is that the code drops the process handle without telling tokio to kill it on drop. The docs now mention this gap. I didn't test whether /bg jobs reading the REPL's stdin cause trouble; the commit says so.

Other changes:
• docs/src/usage/commands.md explains when a job counts as finished, what the note looks like, and the #1077 gap.
• The commands_bg.rs entry in ARCHITECTURE.md is updated.
• The remaining #1063 references in src are comments explaining the fix, and they stay true once the issue closes.
• The commit body lists every difference from the /run and /watch code, as the task asked.

